==================================================

MEMORY TIMING

cycle 1: (control signals are latched on phi2)
	put data in data reg
	raise addr-op
	
cycle 2:
	raise data-op
	raise control lines of regiseter that gets or puts data.
	wait in this mode until:

some cycle later on phi2:
	wait goes low and is latched on phi2
	this means that good data will be ready by the next phi1
	control lines will remain latches until the next phi2

next cycle:
	register operation completed
	control lines drop on phi2.	


The following are the names of the signals refered to as "addr-op", "data-op", 
and "wait" in the diagrams.

op:       read        write      read-relocate-request       write-relocate-request
addr-op: READ-MAR   WRITE-MAR  READ-SBUS-RELOCATE-REQUEST  WRITE-SBUS-RELOCATE-REQUEST
data-op: READ-MBR   WRITE-MBR  READ-SBUS-RELOCATE-VALUE    WRITE-SBUS-RELOCATE-VALUE
wait:    -MEM-DONE  -MEM-DONE  RELOCATE-REQ-OR-RET?        RELOCATE-REQUEST-OR-RET?
